From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PonWrt Maintainers <ponwrt@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] crypto: eip93: check hash length overflow before staging

Reject a request whose byte count would overflow the imported/current hash
length before allocating or copying any staging blocks. Keep the final
post-read overflow check as a defensive invariant check.

---
--- a/drivers/crypto/inside-secure/eip93/eip93-hash.c
+++ b/drivers/crypto/inside-secure/eip93/eip93-hash.c
@@ -302,6 +302,9 @@
 	if (offset > SHA256_BLOCK_SIZE || (to_consume && !req->src))
 		return -EINVAL;
 
+	if (consume && stage->len > (~0ULL) - req->nbytes)
+		return -EOVERFLOW;
+
 	memcpy(stage->data, rctx->data, offset);
 	max_read = SHA256_BLOCK_SIZE - offset;
